Reused implementation and media

The hardware, choreography, clock, weather, tai-chi, surprise, 8-ball, book,
air quality, radio, IFTTT, webhook and Mastodon implementations adapt work
by the PyNab contributors:
https://github.com/nabaztag2018/pynab.
The device feedback, clock, weather, sleep/wakeup, surprise, 8-ball, air
quality, book, Mastodon and radio sounds, the book titles and voice
descriptions, and the choreography files also come from that project, at
commit f24d3e1f7c65f7011e49b55c0e9736f3c13434b7. Their contents and embedded
metadata are unchanged; resource directories were renamed, file aliases were
materialized, and the 8-ball listen choreography embedded in PyNab's source was
written to its own file.
Attribution to the original contributors is retained here, independently of
NabOS's repository, build, runtime and update infrastructure.

External components

device-core is an independent GPL-3.0-only Rust/Linux service, pinned by
repository, commit archive and SHA-256 in image/sources.lock.json. Its LICENSE
and NOTICE are installed under /usr/share/doc/device-core; its source, Cargo.lock
and vendored dependencies belong to the archived build inputs, not the runtime
filesystem.

Drivers, rpi_ws281x, U-Boot, Linux Voice Assistant and their dependencies keep
their respective licenses. Their pinned sources are listed in
image/sources.lock.json; build input archives include the upstream sources.
Raspberry Pi OS supplies the Raspberry Pi firmware under its own terms.

The cr14 and st25r391x Rust userspace reader libraries are independent MIT
implementations from https://github.com/guilhem/cr14 and
https://github.com/guilhem/st25r391x. Their exact revisions are pinned in
core/Cargo.toml and core/Cargo.lock; their sources are archived by cargo vendor.
